# Cloudflare Pages headers.
#
# 1. Hardening headers for every host and path (claims-register finding F6).
# 2. The pages.dev hostnames serve a full copy of the site. Their canonicals
#    already point at https://getpaddock.com, but noindex keeps the production
#    and preview mirrors out of Google entirely. Those rules match by hostname,
#    so the custom domain is unaffected.
#
# Content-Security-Policy notes (src/securityHeaders.test.js pins these):
# - script-src has no 'unsafe-inline' and no 'unsafe-eval'. The site ships one
#   same-origin module script; the JSON-LD blocks are data, not scripts.
# - style-src keeps 'unsafe-inline' because React components set style=""
#   attributes that are written into the prerendered HTML.
# - static.cloudflareinsights.com and cloudflareinsights.com are allowed so
#   Cloudflare Web Analytics keeps working once it is switched on.
# - connect-src 'self' covers the first-party event endpoint, /api/e.
# - HSTS is six months, without includeSubDomains or preload, so it can be
#   relaxed if a subdomain ever needs plain HTTP.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=15552000
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://cloudflareinsights.com; manifest-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests

https://paddock-site.pages.dev/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex

https://:version.paddock-site.pages.dev/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
